# Docs maintenance (Help Agent)

`docs/help-guide/*.md` is the **entire knowledge base** for the in-app Back Office Guide. Stale docs produce confidently wrong answers.

When you change anything a back-office user can see or click — nav labels, page titles, tabs, buttons, role/permission behavior, or workflows — update `docs/help-guide/` **in the same change**.

## Bar for help-guide content

- Task-first: exact nav items, page titles, tab names, and button labels as shipped in the admin app.
- Verify against live UI or `admin/src/app`, not assumptions.
- No schema or code references — written for staff using the product, not developers.
- Planned or partial features belong in `10-known-gaps.md`, not described as working.
- Add a new topic file rather than overloading one file when a feature area grows.

## Help drawer and field tooltips

The same changes usually also touch the **help drawer** (`admin/src/app/ui/help-drawer/help-content.ts`, one article per route) and **field tooltips** (`admin/src/app/core/help-text.registry.ts`). Keep those in step with `docs/help-guide/`. New routes get a help-content entry. See `docs/help-drawer.md`.

Developer architecture notes belong in `docs/help-agent.md` or other `docs/*.md` files.
